{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Bug 57d2-e356-7eb4-4bf5 (theocratic-actuarial-ibex) root-caused and fixed.\n\nROOT CAUSE (proven, not hypothesised). The description's \"tickets branch not yet pushed\"\nhypothesis is wrong — both fixtures push it synchronously and checked before cloning.\nThe real cause: at git's defaults a push into a bare repository makes receive-pack spawn\n`git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach`, a child that OUTLIVES the push. A LOCAL\n`git clone` does not use the transport; it hardlinks/copies every entry it finds under the\nsource's objects/ — the same wholesale walk shutil.copytree performs. The detached child\nprunes entries between readdir and copy, and git dies with exit 128.\n\ntests/_git_upkeep.py already documented this mutator (bugs b394, 5b74, dca1) and shipped\nthe three config pins, but bug b394 guarded only the copytree amplifier\n(clone_topology_template's refusal). Local `git clone` was the second amplifier and was\nunguarded.\n\nEVIDENCE. GIT_TRACE2_EVENT replay of the epoch fixture records a --detach maintenance child.\nobjects/maintenance.lock polling across 30 pushes: 34,319 observations unpinned, 0 pinned.\nPush-then-local-clone loop, 8 workers x 120 iterations: unpinned 5/960 exit 128, pinned 0/960.\nUn-suppressed stderr: \"failed to copy file to '<dst>/.git/objects/<sha>'\", \"unable to read\nsha1 file\", \"unable to parse commit\" — one race, three faces.\n\nFIX (the class): init_bare_remote gains initial_branch/env; 18 creation sites across 17\nmodules routed through it; new tests/unit/test_bare_clone_source_upkeep_sweep.py sweeps\ntests/**/*.py so the next fixture cannot reintroduce it. Diagnosis fixed independently:\nthe two ticketed helpers drop -q/--quiet and raise with git's stderr + cwd — the real\nsuppressor was check=True + capture_output=True, whose CalledProcessError renders only\nthe exit code.\n\nREUSABLE LESSON. `subprocess.run([... \"push\" ...])` returning is NOT a happens-before edge\nfor a bare repository's object database. Any test that walks a pushed-to repo's objects/\nwholesale must pin BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS first."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788622894478462594,"uuid":"56e7bc26-c1d5-410a-9880-3f3cd104390f"}